# SQLite database + WAL-mode sidecar files. bitebox.db was tracked in git
# history before this existed (left there deliberately — rewriting history
# to scrub it isn't worth the disruption); this just stops any *future*
# change to it from being staged by accident, which has already happened
# once. Get a working database via `scripts/reset-db.sh` or just run the
# server — both reseed from scratch.
bitebox.db
bitebox.db-shm
bitebox.db-wal
bitebox.db-journal

# scripts/backup-db.sh's output — snapshots of the same live data above,
# same reasoning for keeping them out of git.
backups/

# Admin-uploaded product photos (see internal/imageproc, internal/handlers/
# photo.go) — user-supplied content, not source.
static/uploads/

# Local dev TLS cert/key generated by mkcert (see README's "HTTPS for local
# testing" section) — a private key, machine-specific, never something to
# commit. The real deployment's certificate will come from Let's Encrypt via
# whatever reverse proxy fronts the VPS, not from this.
.dev-certs/
static/mkcert-root-ca.pem
